# ============================================================================
# FRAMEWORK-OWNED — DO NOT EDIT.
#
# ADLC rewrites this file in full on every bootstrap and every re-run. It
# documents every ADLC-recognized env var. Copy anything you need from
# here into your project's own env file. Commit this file so each
# framework upgrade's new variables arrive as a reviewable diff.
# ============================================================================

# ADLC Environment Variables
# Copy any variables you need into your project's .env

# === GITHUB SETUP (Tickets + Pull Requests) ===
#
# The ADLC uses the gh CLI for the entire per-ticket state machine — issues,
# the Projects v2 Status field, and Pull Request mechanics (creating,
# reviewing, and merging PRs). No MCP server or Docker container is needed.
#
# Step 1: Install GitHub CLI
#   macOS:   brew install gh
#   Windows: winget install --id GitHub.cli
#   Linux:   https://cli.github.com/
#
# Step 2: Authenticate (preferred)
#   gh auth login
#   (Follow the prompts — gh stores credentials securely and every ADLC
#    workflow uses them automatically. This is the recommended path.)
#
# Step 3: Verify
#   gh auth status
#   gh project list --owner <OWNER> --limit 1   # only if this repo uses GitHub Projects provisioning
#
# `gh project` commands and Projects v2 GraphQL mutations need an additional
# `project` token scope beyond the standard `repo` scope — see
# adlc/methods/universal/github-cli-setup.md for the scope gotcha (GitHub's
# own suggested `gh auth refresh -s read:project` under-grants; use
# `gh auth refresh -s project` instead). This is an interactive browser flow;
# it cannot be completed unattended.

# GitHub Token (OPTIONAL — alternative to `gh auth login`)
# If you prefer not to run `gh auth login`, set a personal access token
# here instead; the issue/PR workflows read it as a Bearer credential.
#   Create one at: https://github.com/settings/tokens/new
#   Required scopes: repo (full repository access), project (Projects v2 —
#     only if this repo uses GitHub Projects provisioning)
# Leave blank if you authenticated with `gh auth login`.
GITHUB_TOKEN=

# === ATLASSIAN SETUP (Epic Layer — Optional) ===
#
# Jira is no longer the per-ticket work tracker; the agent state machine
# (availability gate, claim, status transitions) runs entirely on the GitHub
# side above. Jira survives only as the optional epic/roadmap layer — human
# initiative-level status, read by the product agent's bridge and by any
# agent reading Epic context before writing a spec. Skip this section
# entirely if this repo doesn't decompose Jira epics into GitHub issues.
#
# See adlc/methods/universal/atlassian-access-setup.md for the
# mechanism-selection and credential setup (Atlassian MCP server, `acli`,
# or REST API — probed in that order). No environment variable is required
# here; Atlassian access is probed at runtime per that doc's Selection Order.

# === SLACK SETUP (Demo-Video Posting — Optional) ===
#
# When docs/github-routing.yml declares a slack.channel_id, a ticket's demo
# video is posted to that channel as a native, inline-playing Slack file the
# moment its PR merges. Skip this section entirely if this repo doesn't post
# demo videos to Slack.
#
# Required scopes: files:write, chat:write.
#
# A spec-backed PR's merge additionally posts a structured, customer-facing
# update (links, an author @mention per commit author, threaded video, and
# one thread reply per acceptance criterion) instead of the plain video post
# above. The author-@mention lookup (Slack's users.lookupByEmail) needs one
# more scope:
#   users:read.email
# This is a Rollout Prerequisite for the structured post's @mention feature —
# required for any @mention to ever resolve. Without it, every author lookup
# degrades to a plain display name (no @mention); the post still succeeds, so
# it does not block shipping the rest of this feature, but the scope must be
# granted for @mentions to work at all.
#
# Setup: create a Slack App, install it to the workspace, and invite the bot
# to the channel named by slack.channel_id so it can post there.
ADLC_DEMO_AGENT_SLACK_TOKEN=

# Add your project's specific environment variables below

# === TELEMETRY (per-agent / per-session duration and cost) ===
#
# ADLC records how long each agent takes and what it costs, to a machine-local
# store outside every repository ($XDG_STATE_HOME/adlc/telemetry/ or
# ~/.adlc/telemetry/). Nothing is sent anywhere — no network egress.
#
# Enabled by default. To opt out for THIS repo, on THIS machine:
#   ADLC_TELEMETRY=off
#
# Accepted off values: off, 0, false, no, disabled (any case). Anything else, or
# absent, means on. An ADLC_TELEMETRY exported in your shell wins over this file,
# so you can disable it everywhere at once from your shell profile.
#
# Set it HERE rather than by editing .claude/settings.json — that file is
# committed, so disabling telemetry there disables it for everyone who pulls, and
# re-enabling it re-enables it for everyone. This file is gitignored and yours.
#
# Read `adlc/methods/telemetry/telemetry-usage-guide.md` for what gets recorded
# and how to read it.
#ADLC_TELEMETRY=off

# === INTAKE LABEL (per-operator product screening/triage/hygiene scope) ===
#
# Product's screening and triage board queries, and the on-demand board-hygiene
# fast path, cover the whole board by default. Setting this narrows those runs
# to `Open` items carrying one label of your choosing, and labels any new
# issue the product agent files on your behalf (a triage follow-on, or an
# epic-decomposition child) with the same value.
#
# Disabled (whole-board scope) by default. To opt in for THIS repo, on THIS
# machine:
#   ADLC_INTAKE_LABEL=team-web
#
# Holds exactly one label — never a list. An ADLC_INTAKE_LABEL exported in
# your shell wins over this file, so you can set it once from your shell
# profile across every repo.
#
# Set it HERE rather than in a committed file — a repo-committed value would
# apply to everyone who pulls, which defeats the per-operator scoping this
# exists for. This file is gitignored and yours.
#
# Read procedure for any consuming method doc: check the shell environment
# first; if unset there, grep (never source) this file for the
# ADLC_INTAKE_LABEL key.
#ADLC_INTAKE_LABEL=
